  "runtime_integration_review": [
    "Canonical updates lock and reread the latest JSON, merge only the named field and atomically replace the file. Save actions never rebuild a runtime group from displayed fields.",
    "Legacy migration reads existing valid EditorSettings values. Control initialization sets text before connecting edit signals. Explicit settings refresh preserves blocked signals and only displays one effective snapshot.",
    "Startup environment overrides remain separate from configured JSON values. Derived child-environment exports are tagged so they are not recaptured as new startup overrides; unrelated edits and Save do not persist effective overrides.",
    "Workflow updates invoke synchronous cleanup before the canonical write when the effective path can change. Busy or worker locks reject runtime edits before persistence; successful writes emit the dedicated runtime-change signal.",
    "Cleanup uses the observed old executable snapshot without recursively preparing another runtime. Each new operation captures one canonical snapshot; external workflow changes revoke old actor, watch, debug, canvas and catalog context before any stale request is launched.",
    "Explicit environment_changed results make both real operation entries reject once. The fresh-access path no longer treats that result as another access denial and resets the same context a second time.",
    "Personal-model operations bind authorization to workflow Python, combine live unsaved model fields with canonical Node/Codex, and reject late results after runtime or generation changes.",
    "Canceling model enumeration and the extracted detail/canvas helpers retain their prior authority and receipt boundaries. Central presentation still borrows the same live controls and preserves page-only protection.",
    "The latest main pending-action count, board ordering and filtering methods are preserved exactly. They read task state and do not change runtime configuration or authorization.",
    "Only visual notice-panel ordering is deferred during conversation unmount. The dedicated early-close native probe validates teardown independently from the complete node-approval flow."
  ],
